       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The effects can last a long time because the drug's half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nWas this a typo? The usual adult doses are:\n- **Starting dose:** 2.5 to 5 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Maintenance dose:** 5 to 10 mg once daily, which is the maximum.\n\nIf you meant 5 mg or 10 mg, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 50 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical reason. I can then enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
