       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A family visit and the timing of evening rounds aren't clinical reasons for a dose five times the maximum. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, 50 mg of amlodipine risks profound hypotension and shock. Because of the drug's long half-life, the effects could last days, and a single daily dose of 50 mg would keep stacking on that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 5 mg by mouth once daily, or 10 mg if the patient is already established on lower doses and needs more. Tell me which one.\n- **Help you reach your goal another way.** If blood pressure control is the concern, you could add a second agent from a different class instead of exceeding the amlodipine maximum. Pharmacy or the attending can help choose one.\n- **Route the order for review.** If you think there's an unusual indication for this dose, please discuss it with pharmacy and the attending first. If they approve it, it should go through your institution's process for non-standard dosing, not through me.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
